#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: the tradition and its works
#
# The tradition is registered and entered in the same run (prima-materia#924):
# it stood in no registry before. This file declares the tradition, the five
# Stupeni, Tafti zhritsa and the novel Zhritsa Itfat; the harvest of each
# Stupen' stands in its own file, traditions/transerfing-stupen-<n>.ttl, that
# of Tafti zhritsa in traditions/transerfing-tafti-zhritsa.ttl.
#
# Identifiers: Transerfing plus the Russian term of the system in a plain
# Latin transliteration where the term is fixed in Russian usage (Mayatnik,
# IzbytochnyPotentsial, Vazhnost), otherwise a short English term for what the
# translation describes.
#

pmw:TranserfingStupen1 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov, first published by Ves, St Petersburg, 2004. Read whole on 2026-11-13, foreword and chapters I to VI, in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012, ISBN 978-5-9573-2880-3), whose chapters I to XIX run through the five Stupeni; the translator is not named in the text layer. Full text of the Internet Archive identifier reality-transurfing-steps-i-v-vadim-zeland (1704368 bytes, ASCII letter share 1.0, not access-restricted); the text layer carries no page numbers, so places are cited by chapter and section heading."@en ;
    skos:note "That chapters I to VI of the combined edition are this Stupen' rests on a second translation: the Bulgarian Пространство на варианти under the Internet Archive identifier knigi-zip-prostranstvo-na-varianti-vadim-zeland (331508 characters, open; translator and edition not named in the text layer), which carries the foreword and chapters I to VI with the same titles (Модел на вариантите to Течение на вариантите) and ends with the summary of chapter VI. The Bulgarian was held against the English at the reception passage (the dream of the keeper of the reserve, Надзирателя на резервата, chapter I; the English gives him a grey beard, the Bulgarian a white one) and at the chapter distribution of the system terms (махало from chapter II, излишен потенциал and важност from chapter IV, индуциран преход chapter V, течение на вариантите chapter VI), and agrees at both; nothing else was compared; whether the combined edition of 2011/2012 revised the wording of 2004 was not checked, because the Russian scans are access-restricted."@en .

pmw:TranserfingStupen2 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (Ves, 2004). Read whole on 2026-11-14, chapters VII to X (Intention, Slides, The Heart and Mind, Goals and Doors), in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, under the Internet Archive identifier reality-transurfing-steps-i-v-vadim-zeland; no page numbers, so places are cited by chapter and section heading. The Russian scan transerfingrealn0000zela_s5v8 was access-restricted."@en ;
    skos:note "That chapters VII to X of the combined edition are this Stupen' rests on the Bulgarian translation Шепотът на утринните звезди (knigi-zip-shepotat-na-utrinnite-zvezdi-vadim-zeland, 382012 characters, open; translator and edition not named in the text layer), whose four chapters Намерението, Слайдовете, Душата и разумът and Целите и вратите carry the same titles and are followed by a summary and a glossary of terms; chapter XI (Energy) of the combined edition therefore begins Stupen' III. Only the chapter distribution was compared; the wording was not."@en .

pmw:TranserfingStupen3 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe!"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe!"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (Ves, 2004). Read whole on 2026-11-16, chapters XI to XV (Energy, Frailing, Coordination, Forward to the Past, Letters from the Past), in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, under the Internet Archive identifier reality-transurfing-steps-i-v-vadim-zeland; no page numbers, so places are cited by chapter and section heading. The Russian scan bwb_P6-BZN-002 was access-restricted."@en ;
    skos:note "That chapters XI to XV of the combined edition are this Stupen' rests on the Bulgarian translation Напред в миналото (knigi-zip-napred-v-minaloto-vadim-zeland, 358917 characters, open; subtitle Част 3 на Транссърфинг на реалността, translator and edition not named in the text layer), whose foreword and five chapters Енергията, Фрейлинг, Координацията, Напред в миналото and Писма от миналото carry the same titles and are followed by a glossary of terms; chapter XVI (Dances with Shadows) of the combined edition therefore begins Stupen' IV. Only the chapter distribution was compared; the wording was not."@en .

pmw:TranserfingStupen4 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (Ves, 2005). Read whole on 2026-11-17, chapters XVI and XVII (Dances with Shadows, The Dreams of the Gods), in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, under the Internet Archive identifier reality-transurfing-steps-i-v-vadim-zeland; no page numbers, so places are cited by chapter and section heading. The Russian scan transerfingrealn0000zela_h1t0 was access-restricted on 2026-11-13."@en ;
    skos:note "No Bulgarian single volume of this Stupen' was found. That chapters XVI and XVII of the combined edition are this Stupen' rests on the Bulgarian Ябълките падат в небето (knigi-zip-yabalkite-padat-v-nebeto-vadim-zeland, 397907 characters, open; translator and edition not named in the text layer), which prints two parts: first Управляване на реалността или Танци със сенките, with the chapters Танци със сенките and Сънят на боговете, each followed by a summary, then Ябълките падат в небето или Огледалният свят. Only the chapter distribution was compared; the wording was not."@en .

pmw:TranserfingStupen5 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (Ves, 2006). Read whole on 2026-11-18, chapters XVIII and XIX (The Mirror World, The Gatekeeper to Eternity) and the afterword A Strange Reality, in the English translation of the combined edition Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (Ves, 2012); harvest in traditions/transerfing-stupen-5.ttl. The Russian scan transerfingreano0000zela is access-restricted. The Bulgarian Ябълките падат в небето (knigi-zip-yabalkite-padat-v-nebeto-vadim-zeland) prints Stupen' IV first and this Stupen' second, with the chapters Дуалното огледало and Вратарят на вечността, and fixes the chapter boundary. It does not carry the English afterword A Strange Reality; it closes instead with a one-page address, На гости на вечността, which the English lacks. Whether the afterword belongs to the single volume of 2006 or was added to the combined edition is open while the Russian scan stays closed."@en .

pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Tafti zhritsa"@en, "Tafti zhritsa"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, the book on the priestess Tufti (2018), English as Tufti the Priestess. Read whole on 2026-11-19 in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм, an e-book of spiralata.net whose closing page carries the translator's copyright of 2018, under the Internet Archive identifier knigi-zip-zhritsata-tafti-vadim-zeland (file Жрицата-Тафти.txt, 286957 characters, 225593 Cyrillic and 1064 Latin letters, not access-restricted); harvest in traditions/transerfing-tafti-zhritsa.ttl. The text layer carries a page footer for each of 70 e-book pages, so places are cited by section heading and page."@en ;
    skos:note "No Russian and no English text layer was found: the Internet Archive search of 2026-11-19 over the titles тафти, tufti, tafti, итфат and the creators zeland and зеланд returned only Bulgarian uploads and a Bulgarian audiobook. The Bulgarian is therefore the only translation read, one translator, against the requirement of two; whether it renders the Russian faithfully could not be checked. The Russian title was not seen in any text layer."@en ;
    skos:note "The e-book prints, after the teaching text (pp. 1-65), a publisher's note on the fiction version and an excerpt from it, Червената принцеса, in which Itfat and Tili appear; those pages belong to pmw:TranserfingZhritsaItfat and are not harvested. The teaching text calls itself the first volume and closes with a conclusion, a section of numbered algorithms and an overview of principles that restate the earlier sections; the harvest counts those restatements and writes only what they add."@en .

pmw:TranserfingZhritsaItfat a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Zhritsa Itfat"@en, "Zhritsa Itfat"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Zhritsa Itfat, the novel about the priestess and her adventures in metareality. Not opened. Until 2026-11-19 this node stood for Tafti zhritsa as well; the cover text and the publisher's note of the Bulgarian Жрицата Тафти name Жрицата Итфат as Zeland's first work of fiction and as a separate book, so the teaching book now has its own identifier, pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa. The novel is narrative, and SPEC §15 owes from it only what carries a capacity, practice, caution or sign; an excerpt (Червената принцеса) is printed at the end of the Bulgarian Жрицата Тафти and was seen, not harvested. Year of first publication not checked at a title page."@en .

pmt:Transerfing a pm:Tradition ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1, pmw:TranserfingStupen2, pmw:TranserfingStupen3, pmw:TranserfingStupen4, pmw:TranserfingStupen5, pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing"@en, "Transerfing"@de ;
    skos:definition "The transmission of a model of reality as a space of alternatives through which a person moves by intention, together with a body of practice for lowering the importance one attaches to things, freeing oneself of collective energy structures and selecting one's own life line, carried in the books of Vadim Zeland from 2004 and the courses and readers that follow them."@en ;
    skos:note "A young transmission, registered and entered in the same run on 2026-11-13 under prima-materia#924. The author names no teacher and no lineage; the account that he was a quantum physicist is his own and stands as that. Who stands behind the name is not settled in the works read."@en ;
    skos:note "The first of the three decisions SPEC §14 asks for, the contact route, is documented, against the recommendation of prima-materia#924, which expected none. Stupen' I names no source; the combined edition does, outside it: chapter XVII (The Dreams of the Gods) says the books of Carlos Castaneda and Theun Mares describe a model of human perception, gives the Toltec cocoon and assemblage point, and combines that model with Transerfing; chapter XVI cites Castaneda for shifting the assemblage point; chapter XV calls a burst of laughter Castaneda-like. Agreement between Transerfing and pmt:CastanedaToltec on intention, importance or perception is therefore reception and counts once. The likeness to pmt:NewThought (thought as radiation that materialises circumstances) has no named route in the works read and is not a convergence either until one is entered as pm:Converging with pm:compilerInference."@en ;
    skos:note "The second decision, recension and edition: the English translation of the combined edition of 2012, the only open carrier with the whole text; the Russian scans of 2004 to 2011 are access-restricted, and whether the combined edition revised the single volumes was not checked. The third, the number of citable places: Stupen' I has a foreword and six chapters with about fifty headed sections and a summary list at the end of each chapter, cited by chapter and section."@en ;
    skos:note "What the harvest of Stupen' I found, in counts (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl, 698 nodes): 96 practices, 93 yieldings, 33 chains of which 18 stated necessities with the consequence of skipping, 2 series, 68 cautions, 68 conditions of failure, 26 signs of success announced in advance, 6 namings, 1 receiving, 14 orderings by the author. The conditions of failure lie almost all at the practitioner: excess potential, importance, struggle and dependence on pendulums undo the outcome, and the balancing forces are named as the mechanism. No deadline after which an operation counts as failed, and no rate."@en ;
    skos:note "What the harvest of Stupen' II found, in counts (traditions/transerfing-stupen-2.ttl, 546 nodes): 79 practices, 64 yieldings, 40 chains of which 20 stated necessities with the consequence of skipping, 1 series, 76 cautions, 69 conditions of failure, 21 signs of success announced in advance, 4 namings, no receiving, 7 orderings by the author; 99 nodes restate a Stupen' I node with a difference and say so. No deadline after which an operation counts as failed, and no rate."@en ;
    skos:note "What the harvest of Stupen' III found, in counts (traditions/transerfing-stupen-3.ttl, 594 nodes): 104 practices, 88 yieldings, 26 chains of which 14 stated necessities with the consequence of skipping, 3 series, 83 cautions, 60 conditions of failure, 40 signs of success announced in advance, 8 namings, no receiving, 9 orderings by the author; 99 nodes restate a Stupen' I or II node with a difference and say so. No deadline after which an operation counts as failed, and no rate."@en ;
    skos:note "What the harvest of Stupen' IV found, in counts (traditions/transerfing-stupen-4.ttl, 234 nodes): 30 practices, 28 yieldings, 31 capacities, 18 chains of which 4 stated necessities with the consequence of skipping, 2 series, 14 cautions, 19 conditions of failure, 6 signs of success announced in advance, 10 namings, no receiving, 4 orderings by the author; 45 nodes restate a Stupen' I to III node with a difference and say so. Chapter XVII names its own source of the perception model, Castaneda and Theun Mares (see the note on the contact route). No deadline after which an operation counts as failed, and no rate."@en ;
    skos:note "What the harvest of Stupen' V found, in counts (traditions/transerfing-stupen-5.ttl, 342 nodes): 60 practices, 54 yieldings, 37 capacities, 20 chains of which 11 stated necessities with the consequence of skipping, 3 series, 47 cautions, 19 conditions of failure, 18 signs of success announced in advance, 6 namings, no receiving, 4 orderings by the author; 60 nodes restate a Stupen' I to IV node with a difference and say so. The seven mirror principles of chapter XVIII stand as one ordering by the author. No deadline after which an operation counts as failed, and no rate."@en ;
    skos:note "What the harvest of Tafti zhritsa found, in counts (traditions/transerfing-tafti-zhritsa.ttl, 608 nodes): 86 practices, 71 yieldings, 62 capacities, 36 chains of which 17 stated necessities with the consequence of skipping, 2 series, 65 cautions, 51 conditions of failure, 31 signs of success announced in advance, 4 namings, 1 receiving (the book voiced as Tufti's own speech), 18 orderings by the author; 64 nodes restate a Stupen' I to V node with a difference and say so. The book moves the two intentions into the body, an inner centre at the forehead and an outer one at the tip of a felt plait, and builds most procedures on waking into a centre of awareness before acting. No deadline after which an operation counts as failed, and no rate."@en ;
    skos:note "Open, and the next places to go: the Russian text of Tafti zhritsa, for a second witness to the Bulgarian, which is the only translation read; the novel Zhritsa Itfat, owed only where it carries one of the kinds SPEC §15 names; the Russian text of Stupeni I to V, to check whether the combined edition revised the single volumes and whether the afterword A Strange Reality belongs to Stupen' V."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupeni I-V (2004-2006); Tafti zhritsa (2018); Zhritsa Itfat" ;
    pm:corpusWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1, pmw:TranserfingStupen2, pmw:TranserfingStupen3, pmw:TranserfingStupen4, pmw:TranserfingStupen5, pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa, pmw:TranserfingZhritsaItfat ;
    pm:coverageState pm:placesEntered ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteDocumented ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), foreword and chapters I-VI; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named", "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), chapters VII-X; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named", "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (2004), chapters XI-XV; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named", "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), chapters XVI-XVII; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named", "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), chapters XVIII-XIX and afterword; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen'", "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), pp. 1-65; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached" .
